cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AV Atlas: a bibliometric index of autonomous vehicle research"
message: "If you use AV Atlas or its data in academic work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  # Add `orcid: "https://orcid.org/..."` here once you want it public --
  # deliberately left out rather than guessed at.
  - family-names: Caesar
    given-names: Holger
repository-code: "https://github.com/nightrome/av-atlas"
url: "https://nightrome.github.io/av-atlas/"
abstract: >-
  AV Atlas indexes autonomous vehicle research across the complete,
  unfiltered proceedings of major computer vision and robotics venues,
  and reports who publishes, which institutions and countries are active,
  how topics have shifted over time, and which papers are most cited within
  AV research specifically. Papers are classified as AV-relevant or not by
  an automated layered classifier, and citations are counted only between
  papers in the corpus rather than taken from an external database.
keywords:
  - autonomous vehicles
  - self-driving cars
  - bibliometrics
  - science of science
  - computer vision
  - robotics
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/nightrome/av-atlas/blob/main/LICENSE"
